<h1>Questions and answers</h1>

<p class="lede">Short answers, each starting with the fact. For anything not covered here, write to <a href="mailto:{{ site.contactEmail }}">{{ site.contactEmail }}</a>.</p>

<h2>What is FlatSixDynamics?</h2>
<p>FlatSixDynamics is an app for iPhone that shows the airflow around a sports car, live. Drag the speed from a standstill to 400 km/h and watch the air pile up at the nose, race over the roofline and break into a rippling wake behind the car.</p>

<h2>What does it cost?</h2>
<p>Nothing. FlatSixDynamics is free on the App Store, with every feature included: no account, no subscription, no in-app purchase.</p>

<h2>I bought Full Access before. What changes for me?</h2>
<p>Nothing. Everything stays yours. Thank you for the early support.</p>

<h2>What can I change in the app?</h2>
<p>Speed, rear aero and ride height. One slider takes the speed up to 400 km/h. Choose the active rear spoiler or a fixed rear wing, and step through three ride heights, Stock, Sport and Track. A setup-delta readout shows what each stage changes in plain numbers, with no ranking and no claim of a &ldquo;best&rdquo; setup.</p>

<h2>Can I use my own car?</h2>
<p>Yes. Photo Import traces your car from a side-profile photo. Two frames over the wheels set the scale, and the same live airflow then answers around the exact shape you photographed.</p>

<h2>Is it live, or a video?</h2>
<p>It is live. Nothing is pre-rendered. When you change the speed, the picture is rough for the first moments and then settles into what the air actually does, like a photograph developing.</p>

<h2>What is the Lab?</h2>
<p>The Lab holds three textbook flows that every aerodynamicist learns first: a cylinder and the alternating wake it sheds, an airfoil turning the air into lift, and a converging&ndash;diverging nozzle.</p>

<h2>Can I use it for engineering decisions?</h2>
<p>No. FlatSixDynamics is a beautiful, credible visualization of airflow, not a certified engineering tool. It is made to be looked at, learned from and enjoyed.</p>

<h2>Does the app collect any data?</h2>
<p>No personal data. The app runs entirely on your device: no account, no analytics, no tracking. This website has no cookies and no tracking. Details are in the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>

<h2>Who makes FlatSixDynamics?</h2>
<p>FlatSixDynamics is built by an independent developer in Germany. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by any vehicle manufacturer. The provider is named in the <a href="/impressum/">Impressum</a>.</p>

